Alloy: winemac.drv: a scroll speed for games.

Patch 0008 makes scrolling in games work like a Windows mouse wheel: one WHEEL_DELTA per wheel click and per 20
points of trackpad or Magic Mouse swipe. That is right for games where a wheel step is an action (switching items),
but scrolling lists or zooming can feel slow next to macOS's accelerated scrolling. Alloy now offers a per-game scroll
speed and passes it in ALLOY_SCROLL_SPEED_PERCENT (25 to 800; 100, the default, is unchanged from 0008). It is a whole
number so no decimal separator can be misread.

While a game holds the cursor:
- a wheel click gives speed/100 steps; the fraction carries to the next click in the same direction and starts at a
  half, so it rounds to the nearest step (at 50% the first click scrolls, then every second one; at 250% clicks give
  3, 2, 3, ... steps);
- a trackpad or Magic Mouse swipe goes speed/100 times as far (one step per 20 points at 100%);
- each step is sent as its own WHEEL_DELTA message, as a Windows mouse does for each click. (Wine's server still
  merges wheel messages the game hasn't read yet into one, with the total delta; raw input keeps them apart.)

